Negative control for AC-4's READ half — the invoice's OWN assigned payment
method (`mapPaymentMethod`, `invoices.mappers.ts:242-254`).

Assertion it attacks: `invoices.mappers.test.ts` ›
"is the INVOICE's assigned method, not the card a payment happens to carry".

Two different records are both called `payment_details` on the wire: the
invoice's standing assignment (`raw.payment_details`) and the card one
payment happened to use (`raw.payments[].payment_details`). They are mapped by
different readers. This mutation makes the invoice's reader fall back to the
first payment's card, so an invoice with NO assigned method reports the card
of a payment already made against it — 'None selected' silently reads as
assigned, and AC-4's clear would appear not to have worked.

VERIFIED 2026-09-12: applied against the fixed source,
`invoices.mappers.test.ts` went 1 failed | 1992 passed (1996) — exactly the one
assertion above, every other mapper assertion still green, which is what makes
this a control on THIS capability rather than a broad breakage. Reverted
immediately after; the fixed source re-confirmed GREEN at 1993/1996.

--- a/packages/headless/src/modules/invoices/invoices.mappers.ts
+++ b/packages/headless/src/modules/invoices/invoices.mappers.ts
@@ -242,7 +242,7 @@
 function mapPaymentMethod(raw: IInvoice): Invoice["paymentMethod"] {
-  const details = raw.payment_details;
+  const details = raw.payment_details ?? raw.payments?.[0]?.payment_details;
   if (!details) return { id: null, cardType: null, cardLast4: null, label: "" };
